id: flexible
name: Flexible
kind: crafting
slots: 1~2
# A Category of its Type for each Slot, chosen when it is added; each is written into the
# Weapon's Effects as a Category part of its own, and only the one in use runs.
chooses: sameTypeCategory
choosesPerSlot: true
alternates: true
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Other Categories of its Type, one for each Slot: switched to at the start of your turn, until
  its end.
# What it does, for the Effects on its Item's sheet: its Effects line as printed, word for
# word, cut into one line to an effect, each opening with its tag as the rulebook writes one.
summary: >
  [Passive]: For each Quality Slot this Weapon Quality takes up, select a different Weapon
  Category of the same Foundation for this Weapon.

  [Triggered]: At the start of your turn, you may change this Weapon’s Weapon Category to any
  other Weapon Category selected from this Weapon Quality until the end of your turn.
text: >
  Flexible: This Weapon can be used in multiple ways, such as being fit for both stabbing and
  slashing.
  –Weapon Type: All
  –Prerequisites: N/A
  –Quality Slots: 1~2
  –Effects: For each Quality Slot this Weapon Quality takes up, select a different Weapon
  Category of the same Foundation for this Weapon. At the start of your turn, you may change
  this Weapon’s Weapon Category to any other Weapon Category selected from this Weapon Quality
  until the end of your turn.

---

# Switched from the Weapon's row, on its wielder's turn in a Combat Encounter - the start of it is
# the table's to hold them to - and back to its own when the turn ends. A Category's own Quality
# comes and goes with it: switched to Bludgeoning, it has Staggering for the turn.
